---
description: Use @theme tokens for colors; never arbitrary hex/rgb in Tailwind classes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Tailwind colors use theme tokens

Do **not** put literal colors in utility class names, for example:

- `bg-[#1a1f21]`, `text-[#fff]`, `border-[rgb(...)]`
- Any `*-[\#...]` or `*-[\[rgb` pattern

Instead:

1. Add named colors under `@theme` in [`src/ui/css/index.css`](src/ui/css/index.css) as `--color-<name>: <value>`.
2. Use the generated utilities (`bg-ui-panel`, `text-ui-panel-well`, etc.).

**Exceptions:**

- **Dynamic theme props** (e.g. boss round `headerColor` / `bodyColor`) may use inline `style={{ backgroundColor: ... }}` when the value comes from data.
- Opacity on palette names is fine (`bg-black/80`, `text-white/90`).

When introducing a new fixed UI color, extend `@theme` with a semantic name (e.g. `ui-panel-inset`), not a hex copied into JSX.
